{"v":1,"type":"review","id":"01M50K40YYYW7RAE5YJ0G6WMCE","task":"01M50GXCB1T4XHE0GR59NJ5SQ8","attempt":1,"recorded_at":"2026-10-15T20:12:39.2621233Z","status":"warn","covers":{".gitattributes":"045f3a7cfd1c0e507da3e72dbc19b68d5c5ea93b",".github/workflows/ci.yml":"e7c5a379429a9ae5c2434488950af5cfd7e21898","docs/decisions.md":"6715a859c853e11c66cdbc5aba528d5b54f963a2","internal/cli/doctor.go":"f638edef49c948a5606d66fb2e80513adf92057f","internal/cli/doctor_test.go":"43e102a656bc45afb15e768a09cf2b9ba7da97d9","internal/gate/gate.go":"3c8da6c476121a1a1380b30382c0896f3839d2aa","internal/gate/gate_test.go":"55922c3840f4459c796ba74a4398754fa870f535","internal/gate/paths_test.go":"55c3182cd98689d9cd49a387279cfa7fade0c2bb"},"findings":[{"id":"f-87eb97","severity":"advisory","file":"internal/gate/gate.go","line":120,"summary":"windowsPath reads every /\u003cletter\u003e/... as a Git Bash drive path, but Write/Edit go through Node, where Windows opens /a/... on the current drive. With the repository under a one-letter top folder (GitHub's Windows runner checks out to D:/a/\u003crepo\u003e/\u003crepo\u003e; also C:/c/..., C:/w/...), Write /a/\u003crepo\u003e/\u003crepo\u003e/.leadyard/config.yaml is read as A:/..., filepath.Rel fails across volumes, the gate allows, and Node writes the real state file, unless Claude Code itself rewrites /a/ to A: before the hook (plausible). Fail closed: for a Git Bash-shaped path also evaluate the drive-less reading on the root's drive and take the worse verdict."},{"id":"f-08fcb4","severity":"advisory","file":"internal/gate/gate.go","line":98,"summary":"Decision 67 says the gate's path checks ignore letter case on every OS, but containment is filepath.Rel, which compares the root byte-for-byte on macOS and Linux (EqualFold only on Windows). With root /Users/me/repo, Write /Users/me/REPO/.leadyard/config.yaml gives ../REPO/... -\u003e outside -\u003e allow, and case-insensitive APFS opens the real config.yaml. When Rel says outside, retry with both sides lower-cased (fail closed) and add a test."},{"id":"f-ae01c9","severity":"advisory","file":"internal/cli/doctor.go","line":81,"summary":"The lookup probe can fail now (f-467991), but runWrapper passes only PATH, HOME and CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, so the remedy its FAIL message gives (LEADYARD_BIN in .claude/settings.json env) is never seen: a working install, e.g. Windows with GOPATH/GOBIN outside ~/go where the hook finds leadyard through LEADYARD_BIN, keeps reporting FAIL and exit 1, against C4. Pass env.LEADYARD_BIN from the parsed settings (and the process env) to this probe only, not to the missing-binary probe."},{"id":"f-c9b86c","severity":"advisory","file":"docs/decisions.md","line":181,"summary":"Decision 68 still reads as a closed list while other aliases that Windows opens as repository files are allowed and unnamed: subst or mapped drive letters, UNC paths to the local disk (//localhost/C$/..., //?/UNC/...), Git Bash mounts other than drives (/tmp is %TEMP%), symlinks; and for a repository on a UNC share a drive-less path is joined under the root although Windows opens it at the share root (pinned by internal/gate/paths_test.go:20), which decision 66's 'on the drive of the repository' does not cover. Write 'among others' or name them."},{"id":"f-408842","severity":"advisory","file":"internal/gate/paths_test.go","line":1,"summary":"Additions beyond the plan in this round, approved in the round-1 triage or harmless: new file internal/gate/paths_test.go (plan steps 1-2 put gate tests in gate_test.go; kept apart so the accepted gate_test.go blob stays); windowsPath's //?/ and drive-less readings beyond plan step 3 (f-fd6100); hardcoded Git layouts cmd, bin and mingw64/bin in gitSh (f-b70219); the first lookup probe also switched to git status (beyond the letter of f-467991, flagged by the agent); decision 68 now names //./ device paths. The .gitattributes comment line from f-3bffcf remains; the human dismissed it."}]}
