{"v":1,"type":"review","id":"01M50KWXCEPJNP56PV802KMAPA","task":"01M50GXCB1T4XHE0GR59NJ5SQ8","attempt":1,"recorded_at":"2026-10-15T20:26:14.7987643Z","status":"warn","covers":{".gitattributes":"045f3a7cfd1c0e507da3e72dbc19b68d5c5ea93b",".github/workflows/ci.yml":"e7c5a379429a9ae5c2434488950af5cfd7e21898","docs/decisions.md":"4d0fa9ff865c8099e2c335925699d5bc0238dc04","internal/cli/doctor.go":"767c51b45067a79808f1a1eb2af70b2f38797508","internal/cli/doctor_test.go":"b97de28ee2425ae74565c183f9ee70b20a52d319","internal/gate/gate.go":"afe808a5a0f3342aa6871d3d668b60f3fdc2381d","internal/gate/gate_test.go":"55922c3840f4459c796ba74a4398754fa870f535","internal/gate/paths_test.go":"70377f9850e47e24e9e7fd6b17e698845e546499"},"findings":[{"id":"f-87eb97","severity":"advisory","file":"internal/gate/gate.go","line":120,"summary":"windowsPath reads every /\u003cletter\u003e/... as a Git Bash drive path, but Write/Edit go through Node, where Windows opens /a/... on the current drive. With the repository under a one-letter top folder (GitHub's Windows runner checks out to D:/a/\u003crepo\u003e/\u003crepo\u003e; also C:/c/..., C:/w/...), Write /a/\u003crepo\u003e/\u003crepo\u003e/.leadyard/config.yaml is read as A:/..., filepath.Rel fails across volumes, the gate allows, and Node writes the real state file, unless Claude Code itself rewrites /a/ to A: before the hook (plausible). Fail closed: for a Git Bash-shaped path also evaluate the drive-less reading on the root's drive and take the worse verdict."},{"id":"f-07d371","severity":"advisory","file":"internal/cli/doctor.go","line":237,"summary":"leadyardBin reads LEADYARD_BIN only from .claude/settings.json env and the process env, but the hook also gets env from .claude/settings.local.json (which overrides settings.json) and ~/.claude/settings.json, the natural places for a per-machine binary path. A Windows install with GOBIN outside ~/go/bin and LEADYARD_BIN in ~/.claude/settings.json works in Claude Code, yet doctor reports FAIL 'hook cannot find leadyard' and exits 1 (against C4); the comment 'as the hook gets it' overstates. Read local and user settings too (local \u003e project \u003e user), or say in the FAIL message that only .claude/settings.json is checked."},{"id":"f-5b23ad","severity":"advisory","file":"internal/gate/paths_test.go","line":1,"summary":"Additions beyond the plan (replaces f-408842). This round, each asked for by a finding: lower-cased root retry in rel() and TestRootLetterCase (f-08fcb4); leadyardBin, the variadic extra env parameter on runWrapper and TestLeadyardBin (f-ae01c9); decisions 67/68 text (f-c9b86c, f-87eb97). When the retry fires, deny/ask messages show the lower-cased path, while plan step 3 keeps the path as given. Carried over, approved or harmless: separate paths_test.go; \\\\?\\ and drive-less readings (f-fd6100); Git layouts cmd, bin, mingw64/bin (f-b70219); first lookup probe on git status; decision 68 naming \\\\.\\ paths; .gitattributes comment line (dismissed by the human). Not recorded before: git's own directory in the Windows minimal PATH (doctor.go:189; plan step 6 names only \u003cleadyard dir\u003e;\u003cGit sh dir\u003e), harmless and needed for the gate's git calls. No new flags or env vars."}]}
